    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 218 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1001\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 218 of the laws of 2008, relating to\nauthorizing John Lawless, Anthony Akers, Manfredo Figueroa, Richard\nSpatta, David Kryger, Michael Freeman and Concepcion Crespo to file\nfor retroactive membership in the optional twenty year retirement plan\nof the New York state and local police and fire retirement system\npursuant to section 384-d of the retirement and social security law,\nin relation to the payment of past service costs\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation would allow the Town of Haverstraw to pay for the\nprovisions of chapter 218 over a ten year period with interest.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends section 2 of chapter 218 of the laws of 2008, John\nLawless, Anthony Akers, Manfredo Figueroa, Richard Spatta, David\nKryger, Michael Freeman and Concepcion Crespo did not become members\nof the optional twenty year retirement plan of the NYS policemen's and\nfiremen's retirement system pursuant to section 384-d of the\nretirement and social security law, shall be deemed to have become\nmember's of such retirement plan.\n\nSection 2: All costs associated with the operation of this act shall\nbe borne by the Town of Haverstraw, with interest over a ten year\nperiod.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Town of Haverstraw and John Lawless, Anthony Akers. Manfredo\nFigueroa. Richard Spatta, David Kryger, Michael Freeman and Concepcion\nCrespo (hereinafter the \"Officers\") have requested this legislation in\norder to correct an inequity that resulted from the inadvertent\nfailure of the Officers to notify the Town of their intention to join\nthe Optional Twenty (20) Year Retirement Plan of the New York State\nPolicemen's and Firemen's Retirement System within one (1) year of\ntheir employment pursuant to New York State Retirement and Social\nSecurity Law §384-d.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill (Amending S.8058B of 2008).\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThis bill will permit the Town of Haverstraw to amortize the past\nservice cost of chapter 218 of the laws of 2008 over a ten year period\nof an 8% interest rate.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately and shall be deemed to have been in full force and effect\non and after July 7, 2009.\n",
